==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|de|Türkey||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|de|ML.|Turcia}} with influence from {{m|de|Türke|t=Turk}} which in turn is from {{der|de|ota|ترك}}, {{m|ota|تورك|tr=Türk}}, from {{m|la|Turcus||Turk}}, from {{der|de|gkm|Τοῦρκος}}, from {{der|de|fa-cls|ترک|tr=turk}}, from {{der|de|pal|tr=twlk'|ts=Turk}}, from {{der|de|otk|𐱅𐰇𐰼𐰜}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|[tʏʁˈkaɪ̯]}}
* {{audio|de|De-Türkei.ogg}}
* {{rhymes|de|aɪ̯|s=2}}

===Proper noun===
{{de-proper noun|f.article}}

# {{tcl|de|Turkey|id=Q43}}
#: {{ux|de|'''Die Türkei''' befindet sich sowohl in Asien als auch in Europa.|'''Turkey''' is located in both Asia and Europe.}}
#: {{ux|de|Viele Bewohner Deutschlands stammen aus '''der Türkei'''.|Lots of residents of Germany are from '''Turkey'''.}}

====Usage notes====
* Unlike most German names of countries (which are usually neuter), {{m|de||Türkei}} is feminine and takes the definite article {{m|de|die}}.
* Very occasionally, {{m|de||Türkei}} occurs without a definite article; in such cases a genitive {{m|de|Türkeis}} may occur.

====Declension====
{{de-ndecl|f.article.sg}}
* Alternative genitive: {{m|de|Türkeis}}

